      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: IMO, this isn't entirely solved yet. Something like a script you can slap on an object to mark it as \"local only\" and not included in the perf system for remote clients is still needed. \n\nEG: A HUD effect that requires a light for depth and is only enabled via the IsLocal AV3 parameter. The avatar will still be poor as the light is considered for performance ranking even though it's local only. A remote client will never be affected by the light so there should be a way to skip it in ranking all together.",
